# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe-plugin-epuree — the EPUREE plug-in (load the epuree ALPM package at the right time) + epuree.alpm
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: feature
#+DEPENDS: alfe-plugin-hooks
#+BRANCH: master

* Context

Second plug-in of =alfe-plugin-model=, simpler than EPURE. EPUREE
(=~/works/sncf-reseau/src/epuree/=) is an AutoLISP emulation of the public
EPURE API, for BricsCAD on macOS/Linux and for testing. It is to be packaged
as an ALPM system (=~/src/ogamita/alpm=: =(alpm-load-system "epuree" nil)=
after =(load ".../alpm.lsp")=).

* Proposal

Plug-in =epuree= (=autolisp-front-end/plugins/epuree/epuree.lisp=), all
backends, all OSes.

- Options: =--epuree= (activation), =--epuree-path DIR= (repeatable:
  registered with =alpm-register-directory=, recursive), =--epuree-alpm FILE=
  (the =alpm.lsp= to load). Env: =$AUTOLISP_EPUREE=, =$EPUREE_PATH=,
  =$ALPM_LSP=. Without =--epuree-alpm=, =alpm.lsp= is looked for in
  =$ALPM_LSP=, =<PREFIX>/share/autolisp/=, =/opt/local/share/autolisp/=,
  =/usr/local/share/autolisp/=, =~/.local/share/autolisp/=; not found is a
  usage error listing the places tried.
- =:plan= filter: three =eval= actions in front of the user's actions —
  load =alpm.lsp=; register each =--epuree-path=; =(alpm-load-system
  "epuree" nil)=. Engine-side, so identical for clautolisp, BricsCAD and
  AutoCAD, and visible in =--dry-run=.
- The package: =~/works/sncf-reseau/src/epuree/epuree.alpm= (the user wrote
  =epure.alpm=; the project and the system are named =epuree=, so the file
  is =epuree.alpm= — one =git mv= if that was deliberate), derived from
  =src/epuree.prj= (=loader=, =core=, =comu=).

* Acceptance criteria

- With a fixture ALPM system, =--dry-run --epuree= shows the three actions
  before the user's; on the clautolisp backend the fixture really loads
  through ALPM (=alpm-load-system= observed).
- =epuree.alpm= is a valid ALPM definition (loaded by ALPM, plan computed).
- The epuree repository change is *left uncommitted* (another repository,
  outside the delegation that covers this one).

* Resolved (alfe 2.2.76)

=plugins/epuree/epuree.lisp= puts three eval actions in front of the plan.
=~/works/sncf-reseau/src/epuree/epuree.alpm= created (NOT committed: another
repository). Named =epuree.alpm=, not =epure.alpm= as the request said: the
ALPM system is =epuree= and ALPM finds =NAME.alpm= for system NAME — rename
with one =git mv= if =epure= was meant.

Verified end to end with the REAL ALPM 1.0.1 and the real epuree sources under
clautolisp (=alfe --clautolisp --epuree --epuree-alpm …/alpm.lsp
--epuree-path …/epuree=): =(alpm-loaded-systems)= => =((EPUREE . 0.1.0))=;
also ALPM's own plan and encoding check on the =.alpm=. Known noise: from the
source tree =load_epuree.lsp= prints "could not find lisp/loader.lsp" and
=loader.lsp= "core not found" (they look for the installed-bundle layout);
core and comu are then loaded by ALPM anyway. The installed bundle
(=/opt/epuree=) is not covered: see =deferred-alfe-plugin-followups=.
